;=============================================================================
; ddkResignTest.per -- DECISIVE "is my custom AI even executing?" test.
; ONE rule, no units, no DUC, no chat, no timer. If this script runs AT ALL,
; Player 2 resigns the instant the game starts (you'll see "Player 2 resigned"
; / Player 2 defeated immediately).
;
;   * P2 INSTANTLY resigns  -> custom .per AIs DO execute in your setup, so the
;     problem is purely in my movement logic and I will fix that.
;   * P2 does NOT resign     -> your custom .per isn't being executed at all
;     (editor "Test" may not run assigned personalities the way a real game
;     does). THAT is the real blocker and explains why nothing has moved.
;=============================================================================
(defrule
	(true)
	=>
	(resign)
)
